# Aggregate root-dependent spanning-tree hardness

The complete reduction and original receipt are unchanged. Its pending-review header predates the included independent PASS audit. The nonnegative-integer decision version of the exact all-root undirected objective is strongly NP-complete, with costs only 0, 1 and n+1. Intended claimed_solved 2/5, matching the actual approach log. The adjacent directed path-cost problem has a separately developed related literal-selection gadget; these are distinct models, and no model equivalence or two unrelated discoveries are claimed.

Run `python verify.py` here and `python independent_checks.py` inside independent_review. The audit includes a different Prüfer-tree and edge-cut evaluation, with 600,122 exact assertions. No novelty or human peer-review claim. Primary PDFs are excluded.
